# Long Road UI

UI Toolkit only. One scene `UIDocument` on `GameUIManager` — no extra documents for in-game panels.

## Folder layout

```
UI/
  GameUIManager.cs          # host; caches named slots; inits child elements
  LongRoadUIElement.cs      # abstract panel base
  Elements/                 # MonoBehaviour panels (*UI)
  Documents/                # UXML + USS
    MainUI.uxml / MainUI.uss
    SharedStyles.uss        # shared .button / .text
    PersonCard/             # reusable template + styles
    InventoryItem/
    DialogChoiceItem/
```

- Scripts → `Elements/` (`LongRoad.UI.Elements`). Markup/styles → `Documents/` (subfolder per reusable template).
- Do not put panel logic next to UXML or invent a second `UIDocument`.

## Class hierarchy

`LongRoadBehaviourCore` → `LongRoadBehaviour` (`Game`, `Local`) → `LongRoadUIElement` (`UI` = `Local.UI`) → concrete `*UI`.

```csharp
// ✅ panel
public class DayCounterUI : LongRoadUIElement { ... }

// ❌ do not revive GameUIElement; do not put UI logic on plain LongRoadBehaviour
```

## GameUIManager

- Serializes `UIDocument`; `Init` reads `rootVisualElement`, caches slots, then `GetComponentsInChildren<LongRoadUIElement>()` → each `Init()`.
- Current slots: `Root`, `Hud`, `Inventory`, `Dialog` (UXML names `hud`, `inventory`, `dialog`).
- Access: `Local.UI` / `GameUIManager` on `LocalManager`. Add a new top-level region → name it in MainUI, cache `Root.Q(...)` on the manager, use that slot from elements.

## Element pattern

1. In `Init`: resolve nodes from a manager slot (`UI.Hud.Q("day-content")`), then nested `Q` / `Q<T>`.
2. Subscribe to **services / pipeline / entities**, not `GameData`.
3. In `Dispose`: unsubscribe (mirror `Init`).
4. Strings: `Game.Localization.GetMainString(key, …)` (or `(Game.Localization.GetEntityString(key, …))` for entities) for dynamic text; UXML Localization bindings OK for static labels.
5. Keep panels thin — intents via `Local.*` / `Local.Continue()`, no game rules in UI.

```csharp
public override void Init()
{
    dayContent = UI.Hud.Q("day-content");
    dayCounter = dayContent.Q<Label>("day-text");
    Local.Time.OnDayChanged += OnDayChanged;
}

public override void Dispose()
{
    Local.Time.OnDayChanged -= OnDayChanged;
}
```

## UXML / USS

- Element `name`s: **kebab-case** (`day-content`, `go-button`) — must match `Q("…")`.
- Layout/region styles in `MainUI.uss` (`#hud`, `#inventory`, …); shared look in `SharedStyles.uss`; template-local USS beside its UXML.
- Prefer USS classes over long inline styles for repeated look (`.button`, `.text`).
- Reusable rows/cards: clone template UXML (`PersonCard`, `InventoryItem`, `DialogChoiceItem`) into a slot — do not duplicate trees in MainUI.
- Sprites/fonts via `resource("…")` under `_Game/Resources` when possible.
- Motion: DOTween for simple feedback; USS transitions OK for hover/tint.
